  "name": "Kawachi ondo (Osaka narrative bon-dance song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Kawachi ondo is the narrative bon-dance song of the Kawachi area east of Osaka, centred on Yao, in which a professional ondo-tori singer chants long epics of outlaws, lovers and local events for the dance circle. The accompaniment of shamisen and taiko was later joined by electric guitar, and Izutsuya Koishimaru's epics were issued in the UNESCO Collection. The membrane-drum card stands in for the taiko.",
